  "prefLabel": "Rev 3401.13 Pulpwood",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Rev 3401.13 “Pulpwood” means smaller, lower quality timber used with the principal purpose of making wood pulp for paper production or, for raw material for wood products such as, but not limited to oriented strand board.\n\nSource. #10664, eff 9-4-14; ss by #14026, eff 7-16-24 (formerly Rev 3401.14)",
